Description: qtquick: Draw elements in depth, once per eye
 .
 Each element now takes its place in its window's DepthTree: it stands on
 the element it lies on, a popup lies on the window or on the popup it was
 opened from, the top element of a surface lies at the surface (where the
 surface sits is the compositor's), and what is hidden takes no place, so a
 closed menu does not push the others down. Under a modal overlay the
 window's content lies flat. The fitted depth is Union.Element.depth, and
 items carry their parallax for a renderer that draws per eye itself.
 .
 Whoever draws a window once per eye sets the window's _q_stereo_eye to the
 eye it draws. For that eye each element moves sideways by its share of
 the parallax, relative to what it lies on: the whole element, its text and
 icon with it. An element nearer than what it lies on keeps its own shadow
 where the shadow falls; an element behind it is seen through its own
 opening, cut to its own rectangle, so nothing is drawn behind what it
 covers. The moves follow Stereo KWin's motion.
 .
 While no eye is drawn, and in a window that shows no depth, nothing
 changes: the eye transforms are only created once something has to move.
 Inset shadows are not drawn yet, instead of being drawn outside.
 .
 TestQuickDepth renders a window per eye and finds each element's picture
 by exact pixel matching against the window drawn without depth.
